      "message": "Right.. I think it\u0027s just my \"java\" habits are in place here, where it wasn\u0027t really possible to assign a \"func\".\n\nHaving \"func\" as suffix makes it more intuitive to me at least, but I don\u0027t feel strong enough for you to change this.\n\nIn fact, given that it\u0027s actually invoked when used -- category.commandMutator(...) -- and not just accessed as a field, should be quite obvious for golang readers that it\u0027s a func and has side-effects I assume?",
